{"finish_reason":"stop","model":"root","text":"Fetches start in `Runner.run_batch()` at `src/ingest/runner.py:52`. Every URL in the batch becomes its own task inside a single `asyncio.TaskGroup`:\n\n```python\nasync def run_batch(self, batch: list[str]) -> None:\n    async with asyncio.TaskGroup() as tg:\n        for url in batch:\n            tg.create_task(self._fetch(url))\n    log.info(\"batch done: %d urls\", len(batch))\n```\n\nTwo things cancel a fetch: `asyncio.timeout(10)` inside `_fetch()`, which raises `TimeoutError` in that task only, and the `TaskGroup` itself, which cancels every sibling as soon as one child raises.","turn":1,"type":"result"}
