{"finish_reason":"stop","model":"root","text":"Catch the timeout inside the child, not around the group. The `TaskGroup` stays all-or-nothing for real failures, and a slow host just logs and moves on:\n\n```python\nasync def _fetch(self, url: str) -> bytes | None:\n    try:\n        async with asyncio.timeout(10):\n            return await self.client.get(url)\n    except TimeoutError:\n        log.warning(\"timed out: %s\", url)  # the batch keeps going\n        return None\n```\n\nShutdown still works: `asyncio.timeout()` only turns its own deadline into `TimeoutError`, so a cancel from outside still arrives as `CancelledError` and goes straight through.\n\nIf you’d rather collect every failure, `asyncio.gather(…, return_exceptions=True)` does that, but you give up the group’s cancellation when something genuinely breaks.","turn":2,"type":"result"}
